"""Supplementary production directions. Original lyrics, Style and Exclude stay intact."""
EXTRAS={
'SL01':dict(
 note='原版。154 BPM / F# minor；男中音；96 小节。第一段面对合约包装，第二段反问自己如何对待合作者。不要误用 Split Sheet Remix 的三人接力歌词。',
 voice='Use a grounded adult male midrange with a dry grain, clear American English consonants and measured rhythmic speech. Give the chorus a clipped melodic chant, not a scream. Double only the title and selected end words. Verse two should become more reflective before it grows firmer. Any female still fragment belongs in gaps and must never cover the lead.',
 instrumental='Instrumental rage-trap, 154 BPM, F-sharp minor. Short resampled punk-guitar fragments, sparse detuned synth stabs, heavy centered 808 and dry half-time snare. Four-bar filtered intro, eight-bar hook, two twenty-four-bar verse spaces. Keep the first verse narrow. Remove kick for the first eight bars of verse two. A voice-space breakdown becomes sparse kick and guitar, with the last beat empty before the final hook. End sharply. Leave the lead-vocal frequency and rhythm space open.',
 hook='Keep the exact chorus words and the six-syllable No receipt, no return cell. Stress receipt on its second syllable. Make return, learn, burn and turn clear landing words. Leave a gap after each phrase and use short backing answers rather than a continuous crowd layer.',
 arrangement='Keep the trap pocket central. Cut the guitar into short rhythmic fragments rather than strumming continuously. Narrow the verses and remove the kick in the opening eight bars of verse two. Leave the last beat of the breakdown empty. Add one high counterline for the final hook without raising distortion.'),
'SL02':dict(
 note='原版。146 BPM / B minor；男高音；100 小节。写过劳与错过家人，保留明亮外壳下的焦虑；不是 Night Shift Remix 的男女职业对话。',
 voice='Use an agile adult male tenor, close and articulate, with audible breaths and a natural speaking center. The verses should sound restless but understandable. Reserve longer notes for the chorus. Use high female vocal fragments only as brief answers. In the final chorus, let the male delivery become less rushed and more deliberate.',
 instrumental='Instrumental melodic trap with restrained hyperpop textures, 146 BPM, B minor. Glassy plucks, short bright chords, elastic 808, dry half-time snare and tiny boundary fills. Design an eight-bar hook with one full beat empty at the ends of its first and third two-bar phrases. Use two twenty-four-bar verse spaces separated by a four-bar lift and chorus. Thin the drums before the hook, remove kick in the bridge, and simplify the final chorus. Bright but tense, never cartoonish.',
 hook='Preserve all chorus words. Repeat the same three-note Fast-forward cell twice, then separate three descending wait notes. Leave one full beat of silence at the end of chorus lines one and three. Reduce surrounding glitches until the title can be followed after one listen.',
 arrangement='Keep the tempo at 146 BPM. Create changes of speed through drum density and silence rather than tempo jumps. Restrict vocal chops to gaps. Take most glitches out of the final chorus so the lyric about choosing a pace has audible room.'),
'SL03':dict(
 note='原版。92 BPM / F# minor；低女声；64 小节。主歌每行一小节，副歌每行两小节。亲密、疲惫、边界；尾奏揭示完整女声母句。',
 voice='Use a warm adult female alto, close-miked with natural diction and a small amount of grain on held notes. Deliver long verse lines as conversational singing rap, one line per bar. Keep function words short and sentence stresses clear. Save sustained vowels for the chorus. Let the final lines feel settled, with soft independent doubles rather than belting.',
 instrumental='Instrumental intimate alternative R&B, 92 BPM, F-sharp minor moving through Bm9, E13 and Amaj9. Felt electric piano, sparse guitar harmonics, rounded sub bass, dry rim on beats two and four, lightly late hats and subtle room texture. Twelve-bar verse spaces with little melodic activity under imagined speech. Near-silent bridge, a restrained last chorus and a four-bar exposed outro. Keep the scale of a small room.',
 hook='Keep Stay for the quiet, quiet as the melodic center. Let each quiet use two light syllables and a gentle downward release. Leave room after air and care. Preserve the changed final-chorus lyric about remaining present after someone leaves. Remove extra runs and dramatic high notes.',
 arrangement='Reduce the track to electric piano, bass and sparse rim under verses. Let guitar harmonics answer only at phrase ends. Remove drums for the bridge, add just one quiet harmony for the final chorus and expose the complete original female phrase in the outro.'),
'SL04':dict(
 note='两张专辑共用的原曲。144 BPM / A major；96 小节；男主唱与女声回答。六个原资产保持一致。有已选定原音频时沿用该录音，不为 PLUS 再生成一个新 take。',
 voice='Keep the male lead grounded, warm and conversational in the verses. In the first three chorus lines, use an easy memorable male melody. In line four, the male sings Not brand new and a distinct warm female voice answers Theres still life in me. Let the female phrase also open and close the song. Keep the scale of a few people sharing a room, with clear breaths and modest harmonies.',
 instrumental='Instrumental soulful melodic trap, 144 BPM, A major. Scuffed piano motif, rounded 808, dry claps, a small human drum break and chamber strings. Use Aadd9, E over G-sharp, F-sharp minor seven and D major nine as the eight-bar chorus reference. Leave two twenty-four-bar spaces for storytelling. In the eight-bar bridge, move into breakbeat motion at the same tempo. Let cello pulse and violin answer rather than fill every gap. End with four exposed bars and a complete release.',
 hook='Preserve the original chorus wording and melody. Keep Second life, same heartbeat and Second life, save a seat easy to follow. Male lead carries the first three lines; male Not brand new is followed by the female phrase. Preserve the changed final-chorus line about leaving space beside the beat. Do not rewrite this song for the expanded album.',
 arrangement='Preserve the original form and 144 BPM tempo. Keep piano tactile and strings sparse under the verses. Open the bridge into a short breakbeat passage, then return to the half-time hook. The final four bars should expose the female source phrase and its breath. If an approved original recording exists, reuse it rather than regenerate it.'),
'SLP01':dict(
 note='Split Sheet Remix。140 BPM / F# minor；96 小节。Verse 1 艺人男中音、Verse 2 制作人低男声、Verse 3 女工程师。保留六音首句，其余叙事重写。',
 voice='Give the three verses clearly different adult personalities: a measured midrange male artist, a lower clipped male producer, and a precise female alto engineer. Each verse must finish before the next begins. Let the producer and engineer lead the early shared refrain; the final refrain can gather all three, with the artist owning the last I will say we commitment. Keep words clear and ad-libs brief.',
 instrumental='Instrumental drill and underground hip-hop, 140 BPM, F-sharp minor. Chopped dry piano attacks, short pizzicato violin replies, tuned mono 808, sparse sharp snare and restrained hats. Four-bar intro and eight-bar hook. Make three sixteen-bar verse spaces: narrow first, a few bass slides in the second, hats reduced at the start of the third. Eight-bar stripped bridge, then a sixteen-bar final hook. Leave the final bridge beat silent. Tense, controlled and spacious.',
 hook='Preserve the original six-note No receipt, no return cell and the new remix chorus words. Make names and work carry the second line. Keep the contrast between we and I clear. The last I will say we line belongs to the artist, not to an anonymous crowd. Do not replace the remix with the original chorus.',
 arrangement='Keep the tempo at 140 BPM. Let the piano and short violin chops replace the original continuous guitar attack. Thin instrumentation at every handover so all three perspectives are intelligible. Remove hats for the first four bars of the engineer verse. Leave a beat of silence before the last collective hook.'),
'SLP02':dict(
 note='IVORY HOURS。88 BPM / D minor；60 小节；低男声。主歌一行一小节。钢琴与磁带属于虚构叙事，不能假称已录父亲声音。',
 voice='Use an adult low male voice, close and speech-led, with restrained melodic endings. Hold tenderness and resentment together without exaggerated crying. Give I-vo-ry three sung syllables with the first strongest, and sing hours as one syllable in the hook. Keep dense verse lines rhythmic and leave the two-line bridge room to breathe.',
 instrumental='Instrumental piano-sample underground hip-hop with jazz-rap space, 88 BPM, D minor. Original upright-piano motif, sparse warm bass, dry drums and subtle uneven human timing. Present four bars of piano before the hook. Chop shorter fragments under twelve-bar verses; restore longer pieces in the hook. A small almost-empty bridge and complete piano decay at the end. The groove stays physical, the emotion stays unresolved.',
 hook='Keep the exact Ivory hours chorus. Stress the first syllable of I-vo-ry and allow three clear notes. Make claps, back, laugh and have audible phrase endings. Preserve the changed final line about leaving air for missing parts. Do not resolve the story into a grand forgiveness anthem.',
 arrangement='Expose the original piano phrase first, then reorder shorter slices under the verses. Preserve gaps in the drum pattern and let the second verse stay close. Remove the large string pad and any cinematic build. Let the last piano decay finish naturally.'),
'SLP03':dict(
 note='Night Shift Remix。138 BPM / D minor；92 小节。女声掌握 Hook；男 Verse 16 小节，女 Verse 24 小节；Bridge 男/女/男/女。',
 voice='Put a grounded adult female alto in charge of the introduction, every main hook and the longer second verse. Use a restrained male tenor for verse one and the pre-chorus. The bridge alternates male, female, male, female one line each. In the final chorus, the male supports rather than replaces her lead. Preserve her pride in her own work and make the disagreement sound adult and specific.',
 instrumental='Instrumental piano melodic trap and R&B, 138 BPM, D minor. Reordered short piano phrases from a slower original performance, rounded 808, dry half-time drums and few decorative sounds. Early eight-bar hook, sixteen-bar first verse, four-bar pre-chorus, another hook, twenty-four-bar second verse. Eight-bar conversational bridge and sixteen-bar final hook. Give the longer second verse more low-end support but less upper decoration. Leave room for two distinct voices.',
 hook='Keep the repeated Fast-forward cell and three separated descending wait notes. Preserve the remix chorus about working here and somebody staying awake. Female voice leads. Keep the longer female verse complete. Do not substitute the original song about missing today or make the male singer take back the final hook.',
 arrangement='Remove the original hyperpop glitter. Reorder short piano slices onto the 138 BPM grid rather than forcing the entire slow phrase into a large stretch. Let the female verse be longer and less decorated. The bridge must alternate speakers clearly without changing tempo.'),
'SLP04':dict(
 note='COUNTERSTEP。144 BPM / G minor；96 小节；灵活男声。V02 原演奏为 108 BPM 三拍，目标为 144 BPM 四拍；这是编排目标，文本不能强制采样精确对齐。',
 voice='Use a playful adult male voice, percussive in the verses and lightly melodic in the hook. Smile through the scene without cartoon voices or threats. Stress Wrong and Right, and stress the first syllable of Counterstep. Let the rhyme runs become denser, then relax on the laugh. Invite a brief group response only near the final chorus.',
 instrumental='Instrumental orchestral drill, 144 BPM, G minor. Short original solo-violin bow attacks and chopped phrases, a bouncy tuned 808, syncopated kick and spare snare. A three-part violin lilt sits over a steady four-beat drum pulse. Expose the violin source in a four-bar intro, then enter the hook. Use two twenty-four-bar verse spaces, an eight-bar stripped bridge and a sixteen-bar final hook. Rhythmic, mischievous and inviting, with minimal sustained strings.',
 hook='Keep Wrong foot, right time short and clear. Let Counterstep have a strong first syllable and a lighter middle syllable. Keep the title rhythm stable as the instruments shift around it. Preserve the bridge count and the final invitation to join the room. Avoid a threatening drill delivery.',
 arrangement='Make violin attacks rhythmic and brief. Preserve the source phrase triple lilt against the four-beat drill pocket, expose it in the bridge, and bring the kick back cleanly. Reduce continuous cinematic strings. If precise source placement is unavailable in generation, retain the best groove and complete that placement later with the same source audio.'),
'SLP05':dict(
 note='Open Door Remix。124 BPM / A major；80 小节。男 Verse 1、女 Verse 2；Hook 二重唱；Bridge 女/男/女/男，Outro 女声。',
 voice='Use a small adult male-female duet. The male first verse must finish naturally before the female second verse replies. Keep the hook shared and intimate. The bridge alternates female, male, female, male, one line each; the female takes the final Your turn, Im listening. Sing conversationally even when the drums dance. Keep disagreement audible without turning it into a shouting contest.',
 instrumental='Instrumental alternative R&B and light two-step UK garage, 124 BPM, A major. Short electric-piano chord slices, rounded bass, syncopated kick, dry rim and gently late hats. Four-bar intro, eight-bar hook and two sixteen-bar verse spaces separated by the hook. Change keyboard inversions for the second verse, remove bass during the eight-bar bridge, then a sixteen-bar intimate final chorus. Keep the scale warm and human rather than festival-sized.',
 hook='Preserve the original seven-note Stay for the quiet, quiet identity in the new major-key harmony. Keep the remix lines about finishing a sentence and leaving distance. Share the chorus without smearing consonants. Preserve the final line about coming back another day. Do not restore the original R&B chorus.',
 arrangement='Keep the two-step kick pattern rather than four-on-the-floor. Let chord slices answer the drums and avoid filling every vocal gap. Change inversions for the female reply without simply raising its volume. Remove bass in the bridge and let each speaker finish before the other enters.'),
'SLP06':dict(
 note='SOFT LANDING。76 BPM / Eb major；52 小节；低女声。两小节 Intro 即入 Hook；主歌一行一小节，Hook 一行两小节。',
 voice='Use a warm low adult female voice with clear diction, relaxed singing rap and occasional natural smiles. Keep the short title phrase simple. Let questions and replies feel spoken at close range. Hold time and mine in the chorus, but keep verse function words light. Sensuality comes from timing and distance, not continuous breath effects or long runs.',
 instrumental='Instrumental intimate R&B and trap-soul, 76 BPM, E-flat major. Soft felt-piano arpeggio slices, rounded bass, gentle dry snare and a few high pizzicato-violin answers. Two-bar intro, immediate eight-bar hook, short eight-bar verse spaces and a four-bar pre-chorus. Keep a subtle pulse during the stripped bridge. Add only a small extra harmony color in the final hook and preserve the two-bar release. Warm, tactile and unhurried.',
 hook='Keep Soft landing simple and recognizable. Stress land more than ing. Let time and mine carry the first pair of lines, near and here the second. Preserve Tell me what you want with clear words and comfortable space. Remove ornamental runs that delay the next line.',
 arrangement='Keep piano as the main texture. Use pizzicato answers only in actual vocal gaps and remove them when the lead sustains. Reduce bass weight if it obscures low female diction. Keep the final hook intimate and retain a complete natural ending.'),
'SLP07':dict(
 note='LAST TRAIN, FIRST LIGHT。156 BPM / E minor；100 小节；男高音。源钢琴与提琴按 78 BPM 四小节写作，在目标网格占八小节。',
 voice='Use an expressive adult male tenor with clear conversational verses and an open melodic hook. Let the family details sound ordinary and affectionate, not like a speech. Keep the first morning in the new city smaller and less polished. Use light mixed voice for high hook notes; transpose the whole song if the register becomes strained. Leave room for the violin answers.',
 instrumental='Instrumental piano trap and melodic hip-hop, 156 BPM with a 78 BPM body pulse, E minor with relative-major warmth. A natural slow piano ostinato spans eight fast bars, lyrical solo violin answers between phrases, rounded 808 and restrained half-time drums. Four-bar intro, early hook, two twenty-four-bar verse spaces and a four-bar pre-chorus. Thin bass at the start of verse two, expose piano in the bridge and widen the final chorus without a key change.',
 hook='Keep Last train, first light clear as four strong title words. Let the longer response line move naturally through its unstressed words. Preserve the lyric about loving a place and leaving it. Widen the last chorus through harmony and space rather than shouting or an added key change.',
 arrangement='Keep the original slow performance duration while placing it on the double-time grid. Do not double the audio playback speed merely to reach 156 BPM. Let violin answer at phrase ends. Remove 808 from the first four lines of verse two, expose piano in the bridge, then restore the low end for the final hook.')
}
EXTRAS['SLP08']=EXTRAS['SL04'].copy()
